# Hospital Management System (HSM) — Product Requirements Document
# =============================================================================
# Version   : 1.0.0
# Date      : 2026-08-12
# Status    : APPROVED — In Progress
# =============================================================================

## 1. Overview

A legacy-grade, full-stack Hospital Management System built with:
  - Frontend  : Next.js 16 (App Router) · TypeScript · Tailwind CSS v4 · Shadcn/UI
  - Backend   : Python 3.12 · Django 5.x · Django REST Framework · SimpleJWT
  - Database  : Neon PostgreSQL (psycopg3 driver, SSL required)
  - Auth      : JWT (access + refresh tokens via httpOnly cookies or localStorage)
  - API Style : RESTful JSON under /api/v1/

## 2. Goals

  G1. Industry-grade, feature-based folder structure for both frontend and backend
  G2. Scalable monorepo layout (client/ + server/ under HSM/)
  G3. Neon PostgreSQL connection from Day 1 — migrations run, DB verified
  G4. Axios API client wired on frontend with JWT interceptor
  G5. README-driven setup — any developer clones and is running in < 10 minutes

## 3. Non-Goals (Current Phase)

  - WebSocket / real-time features
  - File upload (X-ray, prescriptions) — deferred
  - Multi-tenant SaaS — single hospital for now
  - Production deployment / CI-CD pipeline

## 4. User Roles (Planned)

  superadmin | admin | doctor | nurse | receptionist | patient | pharmacist | lab_technician

## 5. Feature Modules

  Module 1  — Authentication      (login, register, JWT refresh, logout)
  Module 2  — Patients            (registration, profile, history)
  Module 3  — Doctors             (profiles, specializations, schedules)
  Module 4  — Appointments        (booking, calendar, status management)
  Module 5  — Wards               (beds, admissions, discharges)
  Module 6  — Pharmacy            (drug inventory, prescriptions, dispensing)
  Module 7  — Laboratory          (test orders, results, reporting)
  Module 8  — Billing             (invoices, payments, receipts)
  Module 9  — Reports             (dashboard analytics, revenue, occupancy)

## 6. Backend Architecture

  server/
  ├── manage.py
  ├── requirements.txt
  ├── requirements-dev.txt
  ├── .env                        # secrets — NEVER commit
  ├── .env.example                # template — commit this
  ├── pytest.ini
  ├── setup.cfg                   # black / ruff / isort config
  │
  ├── config/                     # Django project settings package
  │   ├── __init__.py
  │   ├── settings/
  │   │   ├── __init__.py
  │   │   ├── base.py             # shared (DB, INSTALLED_APPS, DRF, JWT)
  │   │   ├── development.py      # DEBUG=True, loose CORS
  │   │   └── production.py       # security headers, HTTPS only
  │   ├── urls.py                 # root → /api/v1/
  │   ├── wsgi.py
  │   └── asgi.py
  │
  └── apps/
      ├── core/                   # base models, mixins, exceptions
      ├── authentication/         # CustomUser, JWT views
      ├── patients/
      ├── doctors/
      ├── appointments/
      ├── wards/
      ├── pharmacy/
      ├── laboratory/
      ├── billing/
      └── reports/

  Each app owns:
    models.py · serializers.py · views.py · urls.py · admin.py · filters.py · tests/

## 7. Frontend Architecture

  client/
  ├── app/
  │   ├── (auth)/                 # login, register, forgot-password
  │   └── (dashboard)/            # authenticated shell + all feature pages
  │
  ├── features/                   # feature slices (mirrors backend apps)
  │   └── <feature>/
  │       ├── api.ts              # axios calls
  │       ├── hooks.ts            # react-query hooks
  │       ├── store.ts            # zustand slice
  │       ├── types.ts
  │       └── components/
  │
  ├── components/                 # global reusable UI
  │   ├── ui/                     # shadcn primitives
  │   ├── layout/                 # Sidebar, Topbar, DashboardShell
  │   └── shared/                 # DataTable, PageHeader, StatCard
  │
  ├── lib/
  │   ├── api-client.ts           # Axios base instance + JWT interceptor
  │   ├── auth.ts                 # token helpers
  │   ├── constants.ts            # API URL, route paths
  │   ├── utils.ts                # cn(), formatDate()
  │   └── validations/            # Zod schemas
  │
  ├── hooks/                      # global custom hooks
  ├── store/                      # Zustand root store
  └── types/                      # global TypeScript types

## 8. API Contract

  Base URL : /api/v1/

  Standard Response Envelope:
  {
    "success": true,
    "data":    <object | array>,
    "message": "OK",
    "errors":  null,
    "meta":    { "page": 1, "total": 100 }   // paginated responses only
  }

  Endpoints (initial):
    POST   /api/v1/auth/login/
    POST   /api/v1/auth/refresh/
    POST   /api/v1/auth/logout/
    GET    /api/v1/patients/
    POST   /api/v1/patients/
    GET    /api/v1/patients/{id}/
    ...    (each module follows same REST convention)

## 9. Database

  Provider : Neon PostgreSQL
  DSN      : postgresql://neondb_owner:***@ep-wandering-union-az81w59x-pooler.c-3.ap-southeast-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require
  Driver   : psycopg (v3) — NOT psycopg2
  SSL      : required (sslmode=require + channel_binding=require)

## 10. Development Conventions

  - PEP8 enforced via ruff + black (line length 88)
  - isort for import ordering
  - All apps registered with 'apps.<name>' in INSTALLED_APPS
  - Migrations committed to version control
  - Frontend: ESLint + Prettier (already configured)
  - API versioning: URL-based (/api/v1/)
  - All timestamps: UTC, stored as DateTimeField with auto_now / auto_now_add
  - Soft delete pattern on core entities (patients, doctors, appointments)

## 11. Open Questions (Answer Before Feature Work Begins)

  Q1. JWT storage — httpOnly cookies (recommended) or localStorage?
  Q2. File uploads — local storage or S3-compatible (Cloudflare R2, AWS S3)?
  Q3. Multi-branch support needed eventually?
  Q4. SMS/Email notifications for appointments?

## 12. Milestones

  M0  — Scaffold + DB connection + README           [CURRENT]
  M1  — Auth module (CustomUser, JWT, login UI)
  M2  — Patients + Doctors modules
  M3  — Appointments + scheduling UI
  M4  — Wards + Pharmacy + Lab
  M5  — Billing + Reports dashboard
  M6  — Role-based access control across all modules
